                <pb facs="0793" n="717" sameAs="frus:frus1935v02/pg717"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">611.5231/1014: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Spain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Bowers</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Madrid</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1935-08-14T14:00:00+00:00">August 14, 1935—2
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received August 14—12:10 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>53. Exchange Control Board informed local banks August 12 that it will, upon
                    application, insure against exchange fluctuations amounts covered by exchange
                    applications in payments of imports from England, France, Switzerland and
                    Holland. Unless exchange insurance extended to imports from the United States it
                    might prejudice our trade in favor of above countries. I have appointment with
                    Sub-Secretary of State August 16 and will then cable full report.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Bowers</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
